THE FIRE GLOWED AS OLD KARO SPOKE. LONG AGO AS THE EARTH WAS STILL BEING FORMED THE SKY WAS WILD AND FILLED WITH THUNDER AND GIANT BIRDS CALLED SKYMAKERS. THEY CIRCLED ABOVE THE CLIFFS BUILDING THEIR NESTS. A YOUNG BOY NAMED LUMO WATCHED FROM THE ROCKS. HE WANTED TO TOUCH THE SKY LIKE THOSE BIRDS BUT WAS AFRAID OF FALLING. ONE DAY A SKYMAKER NEST FELL FROM A PARTICULARLY HIGH CLIFF. LUMO RAN WITHOUT THINKING AND CAUGHT IT IN HIS ARMS. THE SKYMAKERS CIRCLED ABOVE SINGING TO HIM IN A LANGUAGE OF WIND AND STORM. TO SHOW THEIR THANKS THEY TOOK LUMO UP INTO THE SKY SAFE IN THEIR EMBRACE. HE RETURNED HOME CARRYING THE SKY IN HIS HEART. WE LISTENED IN SILENCE AS THE FIRE SNAPPED AND HISSED. ABOVE US THE SAME WILD SKY. OLD KAROS STORY WAS FINISHED.